/Title (Telecom strategy refers to actions taken by major network operators to influence market share, pricing \(tariffs\), and service quality. In India, the market is primarily controlled by three giants: Reliance Jio, Bharti Airtel, and Vodafone Idea \(Vi\). Their primary objective is to maintain subscriber growth while balancing the massive capital expenditures required for 5G infrastructure.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 335 0 R
/Next 366 0 R
>>
endobj
366 0 obj
<<
/Title (Telecom strategy matters because changes in data tariffs and network availability influence household spending, business digitalization, and overall economic connectivity. For example, a change in base tariff plans directly affects how much households spend on communication, although the effect on overall data consumption is generally inelastic.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 335 0 R
/Prev 365 0 R
>>
endobj
